      "question_number": 4,
      "question": "In Qdrant, what is a collection and what is a point? How are vector size and distance metric chosen when creating a collection?",
      "message_status": "complete",
      "answer": "- A collection in Qdrant is a named set of points sharing vector dimensions and a distance metric . [S5]\n- A point in Qdrant holds vectors used for search and retrieval within a collection . [S2]\n- If vector sizes differ between points, it is impossible to calculate the distance between them . [S3]\n- The `distance` parameter specifies the function used to measure the distance between two points . [S1] [S3]\n- Vector size can be determined by the output dimensionality of the embedding model used . [S3]\n- Named vectors with specific sizes and distance calculation methods can be defined within a collection configuration . [S4]\nSome claims were omitted because local evidence did not verify them.",
